          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"schema_version\":\"ai-evaluator-v2/1.1\",\"case_id\":\"5-3\",\"candidate_id\":\"candidate_3\",\"action_assessment\":{\"status\":\"preserved\",\"summary\":\"The graph covers the key business activities with acceptable paraphrases: submission, registration, supervisor review with three outcomes, purchase processing, purchase order generation, waiting for delivery/invoice, and notification.\"},\"flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"preserved\",\"summary\":\"The main precedence relations among matched actions are preserved from request submission through supervisor decision and subsequent notification; the vendor-validity issue is primarily a conditional recurrence problem rather than a basic ordering error.\"},\"control_flow_assessment\":{\"status\":\"defect\",\"summary\":\"The approved branch does not model the source-required conditional repeat of vendor selection when a chosen vendor is invalid. Instead, selecting a different vendor is represented as a single unconditional step before confirmation.\"},\"main_error_type\":\"wrong_loop_or_recurrence\",\"explanation\":\"The source requires a conditional retry pattern in the approved path: after quotations and vendor selection, if the vendor is not valid, the purchase department must choose a different vendor, implying conditional re-selection until a valid vendor is confirmed. The generated graph instead places 'if vendor is not valid, purchase department selects different vendor' as a mandatory linear action with no decision or loop. This both forces an unnecessary vendor change when the first vendor is valid and fails to preserve the repeat-until-valid behavior. The rest of the process, including the supervisor's three-way decision and notification after each outcome, is largely preserved, so the defect is significant but localized rather than process-wide.\",\"overall_score\":0.84,\"severity\":\"moderate\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"ambiguity_flag\":false,\"ambiguity_explanation\":\"\",\"requires_human_review\":false,\"review_reason\":\"\"}"
        }
